      In 2000, there were only a handful of young people at the International
      AIDS conference. After a speech made by Nkosi Johnson, aged 11, ‘youth’
      was recognized as an important stakeholder in the HIV response. The
      YouthForce initiative was formed after his death in 2001, as a response to
